  <body>
    <h1>StartSchool Computer Usage Agreement</h1>

    <div class="date-row">
      <span>Riga</span>
      <span>Date of the digital signature</span>
    </div>

    <p>
      The contract stipulates the agreement between Tech Education Foundation,
      hereinafter StartSchool, address at Stabu iela 50-9, LV-1011 Rīga,
      Latvia, registration No. 50008325331, represented by its Campus Manager,
      Janis Altgauzens and {{signer.name}} {{signer.surname}}, hereinafter
      Student.
    </p>

    <p>Count: 1 computer</p>

    <p class="subhead">The parties acknowledge the following:</p>

    <p class="subhead">General Use</p>
    <p class="subhead">Purpose of Use:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>StartSchool-provided hardware must be used for educational purposes
        only from the date this agreement is signed until the return of the
        hardware not later than 28.08.2027.</li>
      <li>Students are expected to use these devices in accordance with school
        guidelines and only for activities related to their coursework and
        educational development.</li>
    </ul>

    <p class="subhead">Care and Maintenance</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Eating and Drinking:
        <ul>
          <li>Do not eat or drink near laptops, tablets, or other electronic
            devices to avoid spills and damage.</li>
        </ul>
      </li>
      <li>Handling Equipment:
        <ul>
          <li>Handle all school-provided hardware with care.</li>
          <li>Avoid dropping, throwing, or otherwise mishandling devices.</li>
          <li>Do not place heavy objects on top of devices.</li>
        </ul>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p class="subhead">Reporting Issues:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Report any damage, malfunction, or loss of equipment to the Program
        or Campus Manager immediately.</li>
      <li>Do not attempt to repair damaged equipment yourself.</li>
    </ul>

    <p class="subhead">Security and Storage</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Device Security:
        <ul>
          <li>Keep laptops and other devices secure at all times. Do not leave
            them unlocked and/or unattended in public or unsecured areas.</li>
        </ul>
      </li>
      <li>Proper Storage:
        <ul>
          <li>Store devices in a safe and secure place when not in use to
            prevent theft or damage.</li>
          <li>Use protective cases and covers as recommended by the
            school.</li>
        </ul>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p class="subhead">Software and Configuration</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Authorized Software:
        <ul>
          <li>Do not install unauthorized software on school-provided
            hardware.</li>
          <li>Use only school-approved applications and programs.</li>
        </ul>
      </li>
      <li>Configuration Changes:
        <ul>
          <li>Do not make any changes to the device configuration without
            prior approval from the Program or Campus Manager department.</li>
          <li>This includes altering settings, installing new operating
            systems, or modifying hardware components.</li>
        </ul>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p class="subhead">Health and Safety</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Ergonomics:
        <ul>
          <li>Follow ergonomic guidelines to prevent strain and injury. This
            includes proper seating, screen height, and typing posture.</li>
        </ul>
      </li>
      <li>Screen Time Management:
        <ul>
          <li>Take regular breaks to avoid prolonged screen time, as
            recommended by health professionals.</li>
        </ul>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p class="subhead">Consequences</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Failure to comply with these hardware usage policies may result in
        disciplinary action, including but not limited to:
        <ul>
          <li>Temporary or permanent loss of access to school-provided
            hardware.</li>
          <li>Financial responsibility for repair or replacement of damaged
            equipment.</li>
          <li>Additional disciplinary measures as outlined in the school's
            broader code of conduct.</li>
        </ul>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="sig-h">Signatures of the Parties</h2>
    <div class="signatures">
      <div class="sig-row">
        <div class="sig-label">The Student:</div>
        <div class="sig-name">{{signer.name}} {{signer.surname}}</div>
      </div>
      <div class="sig-row">
        <div class="sig-label">The StartSchool:</div>
        <div class="sig-line"></div>
      </div>
      <p class="on-behalf">
        Janis Altgauzens on behalf of Tech Education Foundation
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="return-act">
      <h1>Act of return of the computer</h1>

      <div class="date-row">
        <span>Riga</span>
        <span>Date of the digital signature</span>
      </div>

      <p>
        Tech Education Foundation, (StartSchool) confirms the return of the
        Computer and charger by Student {{signer.name}} {{signer.surname}}.
      </p>

      <p>Computer serial number: ____________________.</p>

